-- title:
--   Primes containing the λ-node relations coincide
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and let $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $a\in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, that is: every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ of finite degree, put $A_0:=A\cap K$ (`coeffSubring A K`) and write $\rho:=$ `redRestrict red K` for the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to $A_0$. Let $y\in A_0$ have $l:=\rho(y)$ satisfying $l^{q^2}=l$ and $a\,(16l)^2(16l-1)^2=256\bigl((16l)^2-16l+1\bigr)^3$. Let $B$ be a subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ contained in the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $\lambda(\mathfrak q)$ and $\lambda(\mathfrak q^q)$, and assume: (i) the image under the substitution $\mathfrak q\mapsto \mathfrak q^2$ (`qExpand _ 2`) of every $f$ with $f\,s(j(\mathfrak q),j(\mathfrak q^{q}))=r(j(\mathfrak q),j(\mathfrak q^{q}))$ for some $r,s\in A_0[X,Y]$ with $\bar s(a,a^q)\ne 0$ lies in $B$; (ii) $p(\lambda(\mathfrak q),\lambda(\mathfrak q^q))\in B$ for all $p\in A_0[X,Y]$; (iii) every element of $B$ is integral over that image ring. If $P_1,P_2$ are prime ideals of $B$ both containing $p(\lambda(\mathfrak q),\lambda(\mathfrak q^q))$ whenever $p\in A_0[X,Y]$ satisfies $\bar p(l,l^q)=0$, then $P_1=P_2$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the analysis of the supersingular node in level two: the prime of an integral extension $B$ of the descended node ring, inside the $\lambda$-function field, cutting out the node $(l,l^q)$ is unique. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.eq_of_isPrime_of_liesOver_descendedNodeRing_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eq_of_isPrime_of_liesOver_descendedNodeRing_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728), where the primes of the descended node ring over a supersingular point are identified.
